// Guard's strike — partial damage so the assassin (per the user's
// "stats to autowin a 1v1" spec) survives a single guard's hits long
// enough to reach the king. With assassin hp=100 and strike damage
// 20, a lone guard needs 5 ticks to drop the assassin. The assassin's
// step speed is 0.5/tick — that's 2.5 units of forward motion per
// guard-encounter, enough to slip past a lone guard but not enough
// to survive two guards firing simultaneously (40 damage/tick → 3
// ticks to kill). AbilityId 2 (alphabetical, after Assassinate).
//
// **Why this matters for the fixture**: pre-fix, guards did 999
// damage and one-shot the assassin on first contact, making the
// planner's redistribution effectively cosmetic — the assassin always
// died at the first guard regardless of how many were in that
// quadrant. The reduced damage gives the multi-guard / single-guard
// distinction observable behavioural weight.

ability Strike {
    target: enemy
    range: 1.5
    cooldown: 1s
    hint: damage

    damage 10.0 [PHYSICAL: 100]
}
